---
// Each feature is a CSS-mocked screenshot + copy.
// The mockups are static: what you see is HTML and Tailwind, no JS.
//
// Every tile carries a surface marker: `Terminal`, `Web`, or `Both`. dux has two
// front ends over one engine and a reader deciding between them should not have
// to guess which one a feature lives in. The marker is a promise, so it is
// checked against the code, not against the tile's own copy. `Both` is the one
// that costs us if it is wrong, because it reads as "this works in my browser".
//
// Mock boxes for terminal features are `mono`. Mock boxes for web-native
// features are `font-sans` on purpose: a monospace mock reads as another
// terminal, which is exactly the wrong thing to say about the browser UI.
---

<section id="features" class="tile-filter-scope anchor-offset py-16 sm:py-24">
  <div class="container-app">
    {/* Full width: nothing sits to the right of this intro, so a cap would just leave a hole there. */}
    <div class="mb-14">
      <span class="pill">▸ what's in the box</span>
      <h2 class="heading mt-3 text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">
        The stuff that makes you wonder how you tolerated <span class="text-[color:var(--color-pink)]">one</span> agent at a time.
      </h2>
      <p class="mt-3 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
        Every dux feature exists because someone (read: me) got tired of doing it the dumb way. Hover over any tile for a closer look.
      </p>
      {/* The legend is also the filter: at most one chip active, or none.
          
          That pair of requirements is why there is a script here at all, and it
          is the only one on this page. A radio cannot be un-picked, so it needs
          a fourth "All" chip to escape. A checkbox un-picks itself but lets two
          be on at once. CSS can express either one alone and neither one
          together, so the checkboxes carry the toggling and six lines of script
          clear the others.
          
          It degrades honestly. With no script the chips still filter, they just
          also allow two at a time, and two at a time still narrows sensibly
          (Terminal plus Web leaves what is in both). With no `:has()` support
          nothing is hidden at all, which is the right thing to fall back to:
          the whole grid. */}
      <fieldset class="tile-filter mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-2 gap-y-1.5 border-0 p-0 text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">
        {/* The legend names the group for assistive tech only. The visible
            sentence is a plain span, because a `legend` is laid out specially
            and does not behave as a flex child, so leaving it visible inside a
            flex row puts it somewhere different in every browser. */}
        <legend class="sr-only">Filter tiles by which front end they run on</legend>
        <span>dux has two front ends over one engine, so each tile says where it lives:</span>
        <label class="tile-filter__chip pill pill-xs">
          <input class="tile-filter__box" type="checkbox" value="terminal" />
          Terminal
        </label>
        <label class="tile-filter__chip pill pill-xs">
          <input class="tile-filter__box" type="checkbox" value="web" />
          Web
        </label>
        <label class="tile-filter__chip pill pill-xs">
          <input class="tile-filter__box" type="checkbox" value="both" />
          Both
        </label>
      </fieldset>
    </div>

    <div class="grid gap-5 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3">
      <!-- 1. Bring Any CLI -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">[providers.my-agent]</div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">command</span> = <span class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">"my-cool-agent"</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">args</span> = [<span class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">"--some-flag"</span>]</div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">resume_args</span> = [<span class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">"--continue"</span>]</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Bring any CLI</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Claude, Codex, Copilot, OpenCode ship as defaults. Anything else is a TOML block away. No adapters, no JSON-RPC, no protocol layer.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 2. Themes -->
      <article data-surface="terminal" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 flex gap-1.5">
          <div class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] p-2 mono text-[10px]" style="background:#101018;color:#f4f7ff">
            <div style="color:#00d4ff">●</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5">dux_dark</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] p-2 mono text-[10px]" style="background:#1e1e2e;color:#cdd6f4">
            <div style="color:#f5c2e7">●</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5">catppuccin</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] p-2 mono text-[10px]" style="background:#2e3440;color:#eceff4">
            <div style="color:#88c0d0">●</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5">nord</div>
          </div>
          <div class="flex-1 rounded-md border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] p-2 mono text-[10px]" style="background:#282a36;color:#f8f8f2">
            <div style="color:#ff79c6">●</div>
            <div class="mt-0.5">dracula</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Themes that actually theme</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Terminal</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Opaline TOML format. Bundled <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">dux_dark</span>, catppuccin, nord, dracula, gruvbox, tokyo night, and more, or define your own with eight colors. <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">change-theme</span> live-previews before you commit.
        </p>
        <a
          href="https://asciinema.org/a/1005426"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener"
          class="mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-xs font-medium text-[color:var(--color-accent)] hover:underline"
        >
          {/* No hand-written arrow. This link leaves the site, so the layout's
              external-link script appends its own icon, and a manual arrow made
              two. An INTERNAL link keeps its arrow, because nothing is appended
              to those. */}
          Watch every theme in action
        </a>
      </article>

      <!-- 3. Macros -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">[macros]</div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-pink)]">"Review"</span> = "review for bugs"</div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-pink)]">"Build"</span> = "cargo build --release"</div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-pink)]">"Ship it"</span> = "test, fix, commit"</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Macros, but make them fun</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Stop typing the same prompt over and over. Save it as a macro, fuzzy-find it from a quick-select bar, fire it into the agent or the companion terminal. Multi-line prompts land as one piece, not confetti.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 4. Command palette -->
      <article data-surface="terminal" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">›</span>
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">change-th<span class="blink"></span></span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-2 space-y-0.5 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
            <div class="rounded bg-[color:var(--color-accent)]/15 px-1.5 text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">change-theme</div>
            <div class="px-1.5">change-default-provider</div>
            <div class="px-1.5">change-agent-provider</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">A palette that knows your tricks</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Terminal</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Fuzzy-searchable access to every action in the terminal UI, including ones with no keybinding. Forget a shortcut? Just open the palette. The web UI answers the same question a different way: its cog menu and per-row menus list what the browser can do.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 5. Companion terminals -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">$ cargo test --lib pty</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">running 4 tests</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">test pty::tests::shutdown ... ok</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">test pty::tests::write_race ... ok</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">test result: ok. 4 passed</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Companion terminals</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Every agent gets its own shell session, right where it is working. Build, test, grep, poke around, all without leaving dux. Spawn as many as you want.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 6. Startup commands -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">startup_command = """</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">npm install</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">ln -sfn $DUX_WORKTREE_PATH/.env .env</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">"""</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Startup ceremonies, automated</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Some repos demand a ritual before they're useful: install deps, warm caches, link env files, whatever goblin dance your project needs. dux runs your startup script in the new worktree before the agent even boots.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 7. Agent from a PR -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">›</span>
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">new-agent-from-pr</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">PR: <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">#246</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ fetched origin/match-palette-cmds</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ worktree + agent ready</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Spin up an agent from a PR</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Paste a PR number or URL. dux resolves it, fetches the head branch, and drops you into a fresh worktree with an agent ready to review or push back. GitHub Enterprise remotes are invited too. No sitting outside with the weird remotes.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 8. gh CLI integration -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">refactor-pty</span><span class="rounded-full px-1.5 text-[10px]" style="background:rgba(74,222,128,.15);color:#4ade80">● open #243</span></div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">add-themes</span><span class="rounded-full px-1.5 text-[10px]" style="background:rgba(139,92,246,.18);color:#a78bfa">✦ merged #238</span></div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between"><span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">bench-startup</span><span class="rounded-full px-1.5 text-[10px]" style="background:rgba(251,113,133,.15);color:#fb7185">✕ closed #210</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Befriend the <span class="mono">gh</span> CLI</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Authenticate <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">gh</span> and dux tracks your PRs with open / merged / closed pills right in the pane, opens them in your browser, and lets your agents cut commits and pull requests without leaving the worktree.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 9. Featherweight footprint -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[color:var(--color-dim)]"><span>resource-monitor</span><span>CPU · RSS</span></div>
          <div class="mt-1 flex items-center justify-between"><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">dux</span><span class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">0.2% · 41 MB</span></div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[color:var(--color-muted)]"><span>├ claude · refactor-pty</span><span>3.1% · 214 MB</span></div>
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between text-[color:var(--color-muted)]"><span>└ codex · add-themes</span><span>1.8% · 180 MB</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Featherweight footprint</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          It's Rust. Idle, dux sits{" "}
          <strong class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">under 50 MB of RAM</strong>, leaving the memory for the agents that actually need it. Live CPU and memory for dux and everything it runs, per process, from the terminal's{" "}
          <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">resource-monitor</span> or the browser's Task Manager.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 10. Mouse support -->
      <article data-surface="terminal" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed space-y-0.5">
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">⌖</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">click pane</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">→ focus it</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">⇿</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">drag border</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">→ resize panes</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">⇕</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">wheel</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">→ scroll back</span></div>
          <div><span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">▭</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">drag in terminal</span> <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">→ select text</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Yes, the mouse works</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Terminal</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          A TUI that doesn't punish you for reaching for the mouse. Click a pane to focus it, click a file to open its diff, drag the borders to resize, wheel through scrollback, and drag across the terminal to select text. Keyboard-first, mouse-friendly.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 11. Crash recovery / auto-reopen -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">$ dux</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">↺ reopening 2 agents…</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ claude · refactor-pty <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">(resumed)</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ codex · add-themes <span class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">(resumed)</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Crash recovery, opt-in</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Closed your laptop mid-thought? Flip on auto-reopen and agents still running when dux exited come back on next launch, resumed where they left off. Clean exits stay closed. Not every zombie deserves resurrection.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 12. Hot-reload config -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">›</span>
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">reload-config</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ config.toml valid</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ applied, no restart needed</div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-dim)]">invalid? keeps the last good config</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">Hot-reload your config</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Edit <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-text)]">config.toml</span>, run <span class="mono text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">reload-config</span>, keep working. dux validates first and applies changes live; fat-finger the TOML and it keeps the last good config and shows you the error. No restart pilgrimage.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 13. Provider per worktree -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">›</span>
            <span class="text-[color:var(--color-text)]">change-agent-provider</span>
          </div>
          <div class="mt-1.5 text-[color:var(--color-muted)]"><span class="text-[color:var(--color-purple)]">claude</span> → <span class="text-[color:var(--color-accent)]">codex</span></div>
          <div class="text-[color:var(--color-success)]">✓ relaunched, same worktree</div>
        </div>
        <div class="flex items-start justify-between gap-3">
          <h3 class="heading text-base font-semibold text-[color:var(--color-text)]">One worktree, any provider</h3>
          <span class="pill pill-xs mt-0.5 shrink-0"><span class="sr-only">Available in: </span>Both</span>
        </div>
        <p class="mt-1 text-sm text-[color:var(--color-muted)]">
          Point a worktree at a different CLI, Claude to Codex and back. The current session ends and the next launch runs the new one, on the same branch and the same files. Used that provider here before? dux passes its resume args, so it picks up where IT left off rather than starting cold.
        </p>
      </article>

      <!-- 14. Adopt an existing worktree -->
      <article data-surface="both" class="feature-tile card p-5 transition-all hover:border-[color:var(--color-accent)]/50 hover:bg-[color:var(--color-panel-2)]">
        <div class="mb-4 rounded-lg border border-[color:var(--color-border-soft)] bg-[color:var(--color-ink)] p-3 mono text-[11px] leading-relaxed">
